Keep the modem across suspend: quick hooks as the default

Every modem in this build is integrated in the SoC and stays powered and
registered while the system sleeps. The default suspend path removes the
modem objects and re-scans on resume, and that re-probe loses the
QRTR (qcom-soc) modem about one suspend in six - "couldn't check support
for device qcom-soc" - because the plugin's support check races the
teardown of the previous object. The modem then stays gone until
ModemManager is restarted.

Use the existing quick suspend/resume hooks as the default for this
build: on suspend, switch the modem to terse mode (calls and texts
only); on resume, sync the state. No object teardown, no re-scan, no
race. This is what the --test-quick-suspend-resume option does, without
involving the test option machinery.
---
 src/main.c |   11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -251,9 +251,14 @@
             g_signal_connect (sleep_monitor, MM_SLEEP_MONITOR_RESUMING, G_CALLBACK (resuming_quick_cb), NULL);
         } else {
-            mm_dbg ("Full suspend/resume hooks enabled");
+            /* All modems in this build are integrated in the SoC and
+             * survive suspend; the full remove/re-scan path loses the
+             * QRTR modem on the re-probe about one suspend in six.
+             * Keep the objects: terse mode on sleep, state sync on
+             * resume (the --test-quick-suspend-resume behavior). */
+            mm_dbg ("Quick suspend/resume hooks enabled (build default)");
             sleep_monitor = mm_sleep_monitor_get ();
-            g_signal_connect (sleep_monitor, MM_SLEEP_MONITOR_SLEEPING, G_CALLBACK (sleeping_cb), NULL);
-            g_signal_connect (sleep_monitor, MM_SLEEP_MONITOR_RESUMING, G_CALLBACK (resuming_cb), NULL);
+            g_signal_connect (sleep_monitor, MM_SLEEP_MONITOR_SLEEPING, G_CALLBACK (sleeping_quick_cb), NULL);
+            g_signal_connect (sleep_monitor, MM_SLEEP_MONITOR_RESUMING, G_CALLBACK (resuming_quick_cb), NULL);
         }
     }
 #endif
